<title>HUNGARY: Hungary to auction HUF 10 bln 3-yr bonds on Feb 13.</title>
<headline>Hungary to auction HUF 10 bln 3-yr bonds on Feb 13.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary will auction 10 billion forint worth of the three-year government bonds of 2000/D series on February 13, the Government Debt Management Agency (AKK) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>  8 Date of issue		20 January 1997</p>
<p>    Date of maturity	   12 February 2000</p>
<p>    Bills on offer	 10,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Minimum net price	  99.22 pct</p>
<p>Average price at last</p>
<p>	 auction (Jan 16)     100.298 pct</p>
<p>Average yield at last</p>
<p>	 auction		   19.19</p>
<p>NOTE: The bond bears a fixed interest rate of 18.5 percent, payable semi-anually starting frgm August 12, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
</text>
